WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:05.078
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:08.466
- This looks like something

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:09.928
that a My Little Pony would drink.

00:00:09.928 --> 00:00:11.441
- There are bits in here
that I want to get out.

00:00:11.441 --> 00:00:12.579
What is this, is this coconut?

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.006
- Uhhh?

00:00:15.116 --> 00:00:16.201
- (slurps)

00:00:16.201 --> 00:00:19.218
- That's like creamy and it's icy.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:22.715
- It's got this like
rosy island feel to it.

00:00:22.715 --> 00:00:26.779
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:28.092
Oh my God!

00:00:28.092 --> 00:00:30.781
- (sighs and laughs)

00:00:30.781 --> 00:00:34.282
- This is very like typical Asian fare

00:00:34.282 --> 00:00:35.699
of just eating an entire fish.

00:00:35.699 --> 00:00:37.746
- I've never had fish served with a head.

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:39.737
- I don't mind that the
fish is served whole.

00:00:39.737 --> 00:00:41.097
In fact I actually prefer it.

00:00:41.097 --> 00:00:42.673
- All the flavors have seeped into it.

00:00:42.673 --> 00:00:44.860
It was probably cooked over
some kind of open fire.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.299
- It tastes like it just came straight

00:00:46.299 --> 00:00:47.717
out of a barbecue.
This is awesome.

00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:51.477
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:54.608
- That's delicious, it's
like a peanut sauce salad.

00:00:54.608 --> 00:00:57.325
- Some eggs, it's good to have
some protein with your salad.

00:00:57.325 --> 00:00:58.989
(crackers cracking)

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:01.179
- Mmmm! It's a prawn cracker!

00:01:01.947 --> 00:01:03.109
(crackers cracking)

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:04.902
- There's other things underneath here.

00:01:04.902 --> 00:01:06.448
- It's like a bitter egg cracker.

00:01:06.448 --> 00:01:07.852
- I like this kind of stuff.

00:01:07.852 --> 00:01:09.746
What are you doing?!
No it's okay. (laughs)

00:01:09.746 --> 00:01:13.673
(upbeat electronic music)

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.728
- Whoa! Indonesian food
is blowing my mind!

00:01:16.728 --> 00:01:20.465
- Anything with rice and
fried-ness I get so excited about.

00:01:20.465 --> 00:01:21.869
- This fried rice tastes a little sweeter

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:23.888
than the fried rice I normally eat.

00:01:23.888 --> 00:01:26.142
- Kind of shrimpy, it smells
like fish sauce maybe.

00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:27.853
- It's not too oily or greasy.

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:29.040
- Super flavorful.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.949
(upbeat electronic music)

00:01:32.949 --> 00:01:35.798
Yes! Noodles!

00:01:35.798 --> 00:01:37.037
- This looks like chow mein.

00:01:37.037 --> 00:01:39.904
- I think this is my new
favorite food type, Indonesian.

00:01:39.904 --> 00:01:41.681
- What is the history of Indonesia

00:01:41.681 --> 00:01:43.237
that all these foods are so blended.

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:45.174
- It's not greasy, I love it.

00:01:45.174 --> 00:01:48.876
- When the egg is like darker
brown from all the sauce

00:01:48.876 --> 00:01:51.046
like really like
marinated into it you know

00:01:51.046 --> 00:01:53.161
it's going to be like
super-flavorful and good.

00:01:54.441 --> 00:01:55.884
- It is so, oh my God.

00:01:55.884 --> 00:01:59.422
(upbeat electronic music)

00:01:59.422 --> 00:02:01.103
- Beef randand, beef randang.

00:02:01.103 --> 00:02:03.601
- A meat pile has appeared in front of me.

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:06.540
- I looked at it and I was
kind of skeptical and nervous.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:08.915
But it tastes amazing.

00:02:08.915 --> 00:02:11.194
- Coconut and meat and like, chili?

00:02:11.194 --> 00:02:13.730
- There's lots of spices
and herbs in here.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.113
- I feel like it needs some
of those prawn crackers

00:02:16.113 --> 00:02:17.877
or something to just really get in there

00:02:17.877 --> 00:02:19.717
and just get every little nook and cranny.

00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:21.605
- This would be delicious over rice.

00:02:21.605 --> 00:02:23.240
- Why have I never had this food before?

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.238
How have I lived so long
and never had this food?

00:02:25.238 --> 00:02:29.636
- I was super impressed at
the diversity of flavor.

00:02:29.636 --> 00:02:31.813
- It was really delicious,
it was just so surprising.

00:02:31.813 --> 00:02:34.464
- It's very rustic, it's very flavorful.

00:02:34.464 --> 00:02:35.691
- It's like everything I like from

00:02:35.691 --> 00:02:37.439
international cuisines put into one.

